      "costUsd": 0.006604,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended with this question. Two hundred dollars goes into a super account at the end of every month for five years, earning a steady six per cent a year, compounded monthly. That's sixty deposits, twelve thousand dollars in total. Will the balance be exactly twelve thousand, a little more, or a lot more? Make a guess. You could run last video's rule sixty times, but that's slow. There's a faster way, if you follow each deposit on its own."
