      "pronunciationText": "Take the very last deposit. It goes in at the end of month sixty, and the balance is read straight away, so it earns no interest at all. It's worth two hundred dollars. The one before it has one month to grow, so it's two hundred times one point zero zero five, which is two hundred and one dollars. Now the very first deposit. It goes in at the end of month one, so it has fifty-nine months to grow. It's worth two hundred times one point zero zero five to the fifty-nine, about two hundred and sixty-eight dollars forty-three. Every deposit earns interest for a different length of time."
