      "pronunciationText": "So the future value is every deposit, together with the interest it has earned, all added up. Write them newest first. Two hundred, plus two hundred times one point zero zero five, plus two hundred times one point zero zero five squared, and so on, up to two hundred times one point zero zero five to the fifty-nine. That's sixty terms, one for each deposit. And each term is the one before it, times one point zero zero five."
