      "costUsd": 0.0107325,
      "pronunciationText": "That's a geometric series. Its first term is two hundred, its ratio is one point zero zero five, and it has sixty terms. You already have its sum, from the sequences videos: a times r to the n, minus one, over r minus one, where r was the ratio. Here that's two hundred times one point zero zero five to the sixty, minus one, all over zero point zero zero five. That's thirteen thousand, nine hundred and fifty-four dollars and one cent. So it's a little more than twelve thousand. Five years isn't long, and the average deposit sits in the account for only about two and a half years, so the interest stays fairly small. On the statement, the extra one thousand, nine hundred and fifty-four dollars and one cent is the earnings."
