      "costUsd": 0.0058675,
      "pronunciationText": "Does this agree with the month-by-month rule from last video? Use three deposits instead of sixty. The sum is two hundred times one point zero zero five cubed, minus one, over zero point zero zero five. That's six hundred and three dollars and one cent, exactly the balance the rule gave after three months. The rule adds month by month. The sum adds deposit by deposit. They're the same balance."
